anges:**\n- **Decision record** with three options:\n  - a: stop the other service and start the shop on 8080 before the gate runs.\n  - b: have `e2eTest` start the shop on a free port itself.\n  - c: mark the criterion as uncovered.\n\n  I recommend b, with a as a stopgap to unblock CAT-01 now.\n- **`tasks/CAT-01/tests.md`:** added a `## needs-human` section pointing to the record, and replaced the old note saying the e2e test \"was not re-run\" with what actually happens.\n\nNothing else changed: no production code, no tests, no build files. I didn't re-run the gate. Until the question is answered, the e2e check will keep failing the same way.","ttft_ms":2167,"type":"result","duration_ms":127621,"uuid":"391d6d42-2da7-47aa-8163-3b9ffc09ce09","ttft_stream_ms":1611,"time_to_request_ms":39,"first_content_frame_ms":1611,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
